**Given:**

frac{{sqrt 5 + sqrt 2 }}{{sqrt 5 - sqrt 2 }} = a + bsqrt {10}

**Concept used:**

In such questions we use rationalization by multiplying appropriate quantity to both numerator and denominator.

**Calculation:**

In such questions, solving for the left-handed side (LHS),

LHS; 

= frac{{sqrt 5 + sqrt 2 }}{{sqrt 5 - sqrt 2 }} 

= frac{{sqrt 5 + sqrt 2 }}{{sqrt 5 - sqrt 2 }} times frac{{sqrt 5 + sqrt 2 }}{{sqrt 5 + sqrt 2 }}

= frac{{(sqrt 5 + sqrt 2)² }}{{(sqrt 5)² - (sqrt 2)² }} 

= frac{{5 + 2+2sqrt{10} }}{{(5 - 2) }} 

= frac{{7+2sqrt{10} }}{{3 }} 

= (7)/(3)+frac{2sqrt{10} }{3 } .... (1)

= a + bsqrt{10} .... (2)

Comparing (1) and (2),

a = 7/3 and b = 2/3.

